# IOS Quickstart


Welcome to the Legibility Office Institutional Operating System.


This directory is the fastest route from first contact to your first working Institutional Operating System (IOS).


## Choose Your Path


| Goal | Time | Start |
|---|---:|---|
| Understand IOS | 15 min | `quickstart-15-minutes.md` |
| Build a basic institution | 30 min | `quickstart-30-minutes.md` |
| Build a complete IOS | 60 min | `quickstart-60-minutes.md` |
| Understand the architecture | 15 min | `first-ios.md` |
| Choose an implementation | 5 min | `choose-your-path.md` |


## The IOS Model


Policy Intent
↓
Governance Architecture
↓
Procurement Systems
↓
Institutional Capability
↓
Execution Capacity
↓
Public Value


The objective is not to produce another policy document.


The objective is to create an institutional system that can continuously learn, coordinate, execute, and create public value.


## Start Here


If this is your first time:


1. Read `choose-your-path.md`.
2. Select Country, Ministry, or Agency.
3. Open the corresponding example in `examples/`.
4. Complete the templates.
5. Connect the institution to the Knowledge Graph.
6. Validate the result.
7. Record the first institutional signals.
8. Publish your IOS.


## What You Will Build


A basic IOS contains:


- Institution profile
- Governance model
- Procurement model
- Capability map
- DPI dependencies
- Risk register
- Institutional memory
- Initial signals
- Institutional relationships
- Improvement roadmap


## Core Principle


> Projects deliver outputs. Institutional Operating Systems repeatedly generate outcomes.
